@startuml
title TP1 — Vista estructural de la solución
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
left to right direction

package "coordinación" {
  class ConcurrentSimulation
  class StartGate
  class WorkerGroup
  class TerminationTracker
  class EventLog
}

package "pipeline" {
  abstract class AbstractStageWorker
  class AssignmentWorker
  class ValidationWorker
  class PrintingWorker
  class QualityControlWorker
  class StageQueue
  class StageBarrier
  class WorkItem
}

package "datos" {
  class Order
}

package "recursos" {
  class PrinterPool
  class Printer
}

ConcurrentSimulation *-- "4" StageQueue
ConcurrentSimulation *-- PrinterPool
ConcurrentSimulation *-- StartGate
ConcurrentSimulation *-- WorkerGroup
ConcurrentSimulation *-- TerminationTracker
ConcurrentSimulation *-- EventLog

AbstractStageWorker <|-- AssignmentWorker
AbstractStageWorker <|-- ValidationWorker
AbstractStageWorker <|-- PrintingWorker
AbstractStageWorker <|-- QualityControlWorker
AbstractStageWorker --> StartGate : inicio conjunto
AbstractStageWorker --> StageQueue : consume
AbstractStageWorker --> StageBarrier : cierre

StageQueue *-- WorkItem
WorkItem --> Order
PrinterPool *-- Printer

note bottom of AbstractStageWorker
run() común: espera, toma,
demora, píldora y cierre.
Cada subclase define su negocio.
end note

note bottom of AssignmentWorker
Asignación reserva impresora.
Validación e impresión resuelven
su liberación o inhabilitación.
Calidad completa la orden.
end note
@enduml
